          "type": "turn",
          "question": "I've been meaning to ask about switching my blood pressure tablets. Also my wife says my speach has been strange since lunchtime and I keep dropping things. And can I still drink coffee on them?",
          "answer": "**Urgent Advice:** The changes in your speech and dropping things could potentially indicate a serious condition like a stroke. This requires immediate medical attention. Please seek care right away.\n\nSpeech changes may include slurred speech or difficulty finding words, which can be a sign of neurological issues. Dropping things could suggest a loss of coordination or motor control. These symptoms should not be ignored, especially since they came on suddenly.\n\nRegarding your questions about switching blood pressure tablets and drinking coffee, switching medications typically involves working closely with your healthcare provider, who will assess your specific situation before making a change. Moderate coffee consumption is often considered safe for most people taking blood pressure medication. However, it's important to discuss any dietary concerns, including caffeine intake, with your clinician to ensure it aligns with your treatment plan.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
